        <div id="monitors-vs-kits" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">
            4. Continuous Monitors vs Charcoal Test Kits
          </h2>

          <p>
            There are two broad ways to measure radon at home, and they answer slightly different questions. A charcoal kit is a sealed canister of activated charcoal that absorbs radon for a few days; you mail it to a lab, which counts the decay products and reports one average for that window. A continuous monitor is an electronic device with a sensing chamber that counts radon decays all day, every day, and keeps a running average for as long as it is switched on.
          </p>

          <div class="overflow-hidden border border-gray-200 rounded-2xl my-8">
            <div class="overflow-x-auto">
              <table class="w-full text-left">
