          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            For most homes, the Airthings Corentium Home 2 is the right radon detector: battery powered so it goes in the correct spot, a screen that shows the long-term average without an app, and a sensor with a long track record. If you want to watch radon move hour by hour, or verify a new mitigation system quickly, the RadonEye RD200 is the better tool.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Whatever you buy, the method matters more than the model. Test on the lowest lived-in level, let the detector run through a heating season, and make your decision on the long-term average. Below 2 pCi/L, relax. Between 2 and 4, weigh it. At 4 or above, call a certified mitigator and keep the monitor running afterward to prove the fix works.
